WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.235
Lawmakers have reached a deal

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.070
to avoid another
government shutdown,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.339
but President Trump says
he's not happy with it.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.808
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:13.313
♪♪

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.548
If there's one thing
we've learned about Donald Trump

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.250
in the two years
he's been president,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.319
it's that you can't negotiate
with him,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.921
which is ironic considering
that was his whole thing

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:24.123
he was supposed to be --

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.692
a great dealmaker who could
bring everyone together.

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.327
Although,
even during the campaign,

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.262
there were hints
that he didn't really know

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.730
what he was talking about.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.066
-With Congress, you have to get
everybody in a room,

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.536
and you have to
get them to agree,

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.337
but you have to get them
to agree what you want,

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.407
and that's part
of being a dealmaker.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:44.009
You have to get people in,
grab them, hug them, kiss them,

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.378
and get the deal done,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.014
but it's got to be the deal
that you want.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.650
-What are you talking about?

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.486
I mean, we all know you didn't
write "The Art of the Deal,"

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.556
but did you not even read it?

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.258
I mean, I'm just imagining
Trump chasing Chuck Schumer

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.260
around the Oval Office
trying to hug him.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.229
"Come here, Chuck!

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.431
We got to make a deal, Chuck!"

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.401
[ Applause ]

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.803
Now...

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:14.207
if Trump kissed Mitch McConnell,
on the other hand,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.643
he might finally
turn into a prince.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.178
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.414
Also, what you're describing
is not a deal.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.316
What you're describing
is a Benny Hill sketch...

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:27.219
which is, I guess, why
you have the same hair.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.055
This keeps happening.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.689
For two years,
Trump has said in public

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:32.725
that he wants to make a deal,
but then, in reality,

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.794
he has neither the ability
to negotiate, nor the interest.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:37.196
For example, you might remember

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.532
that after Trump unilaterally
subjected the country

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.200
to the longest government
shutdown in history,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.670
forcing workers to go
without paychecks,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.971
he claimed the one thing
he had gotten in his deal

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:47.674
with the Democrats
was an agreement

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.176
to negotiate over the wall,
although, as usual,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.644
he was very hung up

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.380
on what words we should use
to describe the wall.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:00.286
-I have seen and heard from
enough Democrats and Republicans

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:05.024
that they are willing
to put partisanship aside.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:09.195
They have said they are for
complete border security,

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.299
and they have finally
and fully acknowledged

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:17.169
that having barriers,
fencing, or walls,

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.973
or whatever
you want to call it...

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.108
-How can you negotiate
for something

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.810
when you don't even know
what it is?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.180
You know, people say Trump
doesn't work very hard,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.916
but he's clearly spent a lot
of time sitting in his office,

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.319
typing the word "wall"
into a thesaurus.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.321
"Call it whatever you want.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.156
Barriers, fencing...

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.759
fortifications...

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.361
enclosures...

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:45.331
parapets."

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.667
So, that was Trump's big
announcement after the shutdown,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.702
that lawmakers from both sides
would get together

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.437
and come up with a deal
that would avoid

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.506
another government shutdown
by the end of the week.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.074
So how's that going?
Well, on Monday night,

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.409
Trump was asked for an update
on the negotiations

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:58.844
during an interview on Fox News

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:01.014
and said he wasn't
following the negotiations

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.517
because he was spending his time
doing interviews on Fox News.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.920
-Mr. President, word broke
late today, early this evening

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.789
that there might be
some tentative deal struck

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:12.324
to avert a government shutdown.

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:13.959
What can you tell us?

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.929
-Well, I can tell you that
a lot of things have changed,

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.196
and we'll see what happens.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.165
I can't go into the exact deal.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.300
I just heard it very quickly,
coming over to see you.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.571
It was between the deal and you,
and I had to choose you.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:27.973
-He literally said,

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:30.543
"I had a choice between
running the government

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:34.413
and going on Fox News,
and I chose Fox News."

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.749
No quote has ever summed up
Trump's presidency

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.017
better than that.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.020
Also, anyone can
get on Fox News.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.823
It's not some exclusive
high-end night club.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:47.360
Last week, they put this guy
on TV to talk about healthcare.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.930
-I have eternal healthcare,
and it's free.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.099
Doctors can give you
a little temporary reprieve,

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:56.969
but they cannot save you
from physical death.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.939
The doctors who treat you,
they die, too.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.773
-That guy wasn't even
in New York.

00:04:01.773 --> 00:04:05.311
They just brought a camera
to his shack in the woods.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.248
So, Trump made a big show of
championing the bipartisan talks

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.182
after he caved
in the shutdown fight,

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.718
and now he says he's not even
paying attention to them,

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.054
which might explain why
when he found out that the deal

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.557
didn't have any money for a
concrete border wall yesterday,

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.191
he said he wasn't happy with it.

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:21.461
Although, he didn't even
really seem to know

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:23.563
what he wanted
or what he was upset about.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.965
-Sir, will you sign
Congress' border deal?

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.167
-I have to study it.
I'm not happy about it.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.938
It's not doing the trick,
but I'm adding things to it,

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:34.339
and when you add
whatever I have to add,

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:38.177
it's all going to happen.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:43.783
-He has all the specificity
of a "Real Housewives" promo.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:48.988
"When you add whatever I have to
add, it's all going to happen."

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.491
[ Applause ]

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:57.863
I mean, I hope he's never
the only eyewitness to a crime.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:02.335
"Yeah, it was a person somewhere
between 3 and 10 feet tall.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:07.806
Two legs. Oh, and clothes!
He had clothes on. Or she."

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:11.744
Trump talks about the wall
like he just ran into one.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.512
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.281
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.750
Every few months --
Every few months,

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.518
we have to go through
this exhausting ritual

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:21.287
where we pretend the President
actually knows

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.756
what he's talking about, even
though it's clear he doesn't.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.558
The negotiations over the wall

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:28.828
are just like the negotiations
over healthcare in 2017

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.830
when Trump kept saying
he wanted Democrats

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.898
to work with him
on the GOP healthcare bill

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:35.101
but also made clear
he had no idea

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.236
what was in the
GOP healthcare bill.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.839
-We had to go with
the healthcare first,

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:42.174
and we're doing well.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.477
I think we're going to have
some great surprises.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.512
We are looking at a healthcare

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:51.050
that would be a fantastic
tribute to our country,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.752
a healthcare that will
take care of people finally

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:57.690
for the right reasons
and also at the right cost.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.692
This will be a plan where
you can choose your doctor.

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:03.562
This will be a plan
where you can choose your plan,

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:04.930
and you know what the plan is.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.699
This is the plan.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:10.836
"I call it...
the plan, plan, plan."

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:13.172
Every time he talks
about something complicated,

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.108
it's like an episode
of "Seinfeld"

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:18.177
where George is trying
to get fired.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.412
"I have a plan, Jerry!"
"What's the plan?"

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:22.682
"It's a plan where
you can choose your plan!"

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.017
"And you think you'll get away
with this plan?"

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.953
"That's the plan!"
"Well, that's a hell of a plan."

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.056
[ "Seinfeld" theme plays ]

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:32.358
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:37.630
Yesterday, Trump tried to argue

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.933
that the wall was already
being built, which is not true.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.569
And he even claimed he was
making old sections of the wall

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.404
look beautiful
by repainting them.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:49.474
-We're getting
a beautiful-looking structure,

00:06:49.474 --> 00:06:51.610
because it was crazy
what they were putting up.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.512
In fact, I happen to think
that the walls

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:56.248
that they were building were
so unattractive and so ugly,

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:59.552
that walls got bad names, okay,
if that means anything.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:02.121
-No, it doesn't.
It doesn't mean anything to us.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.957
Walls didn't have bad names.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:08.293
Walls had no names.

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:13.165
Before you showed up, we never
talked about walls at all.

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:17.369
And we certainly
never chanted about them.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:20.206
Trump then continued to insist
that the wall was being built

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:22.875
while simultaneously complaining
that he was mad that Congress

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.677
wasn't giving him money
to build the wall.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.611
And it was impossible to follow.

00:07:26.611 --> 00:07:29.281
See if you understand
what he is talking about here.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:33.018
-I can tell that you that --
Am I happy at first glance?

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:34.587
I just got to see it.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:38.524
The answer is, no, I'm not.
I'm not happy.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.960
But am I happy with where
we're going? I'm thrilled.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.162
Because we're
supplementing things

00:07:44.162 --> 00:07:45.898
and moving things around,

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.134
and we're doing things
that are fantastic.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.436
-In the span of 20 seconds,
he went from saying

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.504
he was not happy
to saying he was thrilled

00:07:52.504 --> 00:07:55.308
to saying he was doing things
that are fantastic.

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.109
If we just let him keep talking,

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.879
he'll say he's building
the wall, he built the wall,
everyone loves the wall,

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.480
and he's moving
to the southern border

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.782
to live in a one-bedroom
apartment with his
best friend, The Wall.

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:07.052
We're going to film it
for a TV show and call it
"Wall and Grace."

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:09.522
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.995
We are in this situation because
Trump sold his supporters

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.330
an obvious lie he had
no intention of keeping,

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.800
and now he's desperately trying
to save face.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.468
For example, now he's just lying

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.270
and saying the wall
is already getting built.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.738
In fact, he even said recently
that his supporters should start

00:08:26.738 --> 00:08:28.940
chanting "finish the wall"
rather than "build the wall."

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.176
But judging from his rally
in Texas on Monday,

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:33.278
his supporters didn't
exactly hear the news.

00:08:33.278 --> 00:08:35.380
-We're building the wall.
A lot of it has --

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.683
I mean, the chant now
should be "finish the wall"

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:39.018
as opposed to "build the wall."

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:40.686
'Cause we're building
a lot of wall.

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:43.588
-Build that wall!
Build that wall!

00:08:43.588 --> 00:08:46.458
Build that wall!
Build that wall!

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:50.863
-Even your supporters know that
you haven't started the wall.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.798
Because they know, if you had,

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:56.002
Fox News would have a camera
pointed at it 24/7,

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:59.972
and the foreman on the job would
be the fourth Fox and Friend.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.240
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:05.010
In fact, after that chant --
after that chant,

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.913
Trump tried to tell the crowd
that they were wrong.

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.216
-You really mean
"finish that wall,"

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:12.784
because we've built a lot of it.
It's "finish that wall."

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:14.653
-He's like the world's
[bleep] hypnotist.

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.756
"You're a chicken."
"What are you talking about?"

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:19.992
"Stop talking.
Chickens don't talk."

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:23.829
This is the lesson
of Trump's presidency so far.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.197
You can't negotiate with someone

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:26.865
who inhabits a different reality
than you do.

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:29.534
Trump spends all day
digesting lies from Fox News.

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:32.438
Fox News, in turn, reinforces
his alternate reality.

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:35.074
In fact, Fox News
has been insisting for weeks

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:37.075
that even though Trump didn't
get any money for his wall,

00:09:37.075 --> 00:09:39.011
in the end
he'll find a way to win.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:40.479
-Anyone out there, by the way,

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.348
thinking President Trump
caved today,

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.550
you don't really know
the Donald Trump I know.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.519
He right now holds
all the cards.

00:09:46.519 --> 00:09:48.321
-I think the President's
probably going to say,

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:50.456
"You know what? I'm going to
take that number right there.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:54.426
$1.4 billion
for 55 miles of border wall."

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:57.363
And then I bet he's got
something up his sleeve.

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.364
-If Trump ever has anything
up his sleeve,

00:09:59.364 --> 00:10:02.368
it's a cheeseburger
that somehow got stuck there.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.902
He just hasn't found it yet.

00:10:03.902 --> 00:10:07.873
"What the hell is --
Ohh! Hello, friend!"

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.575
Trump sold his voters
an obvious lie

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:11.276
that he had no intention
of keeping,

00:10:11.276 --> 00:10:13.745
and now he's concocting
more lies to justify
the original lie.

00:10:13.745 --> 00:10:15.147
He's never going to
get his wall.

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:16.982
He doesn't even have a plan
for getting his wall.

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:19.251
If you ask him to describe
his plan, he'd say...

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.186
-You know what the plan is.
This is the plan.

00:10:21.186 --> 00:10:23.756
-This has been "A Closer Look."

